questions.response:
He is called **Christ** (“Anointed”) because God the Father ordained Him and anointed Him with the Holy Spirit to be:

- **Our chief Prophet and Teacher**, who fully reveals God’s will for our salvation;
- **Our only High Priest**, who redeemed us by His one sacrifice and continually intercedes for us;
- **Our eternal King**, who governs us by His Word and Spirit and defends and preserves us in His salvation.

The Scriptures manifest themselves to be the Word of God:

- by their **majesty** and **purity**;
- by the **consent of all the parts**;
- by the **scope of the whole**, which is to give all glory to God;
- by their **light and power** to convince and convert sinners, and to comfort and build up believers unto salvation.

Yet the **Spirit of God**, bearing witness by and with the Scriptures in the heart of man, is alone able fully to persuade that they are the very Word of God.

It was requisite that the Mediator should be **God** so that he might:

- Sustain and keep the human nature from sinking under God’s infinite wrath and the power of death;
- Give infinite worth and efficacy to his obedience, sufferings, and intercession;
- Satisfy God’s justice;
- Procure God’s favor;
- Purchase a people for himself;
- Give them his Spirit;
- Conquer all their enemies;
- And bring them to everlasting salvation.

